    hint: 
  caseFiles:
  - title: Case Notes
    body: "\u2022 You have not ordered anything this month."
  - title: How This Room Works
    body: 'Six questions are waiting in this room. They arrive one at a time, in
      a different order on every attempt.


      Case questions have four answer
      choices, shuffled each attempt. Pick the safest and most accurate one.


      Messages
      and web pages are judged as SCAM or LEGITIMATE.


      Score 380 or more to
      unlock the next room.'
  firstMessageDelay: 8
  delayBetweenMessages: {x: 10, y: 20}
  minimumActivityDelay: 4
  scoring:
    basePoints: 100
    speedBonus: 0
    fastWindow: 0.35
    wrongPenalty: 10
    recoveryPoints: 20
    baseReadingSeconds: 25
    secondsPerWord: 0.6
    secondsPerDetail: 4
    minReadingSeconds: 45
    maxReadingSeconds: 150
    caseExtraSeconds: 60
    overtimeStepSeconds: 15
    overtimePenaltyPerStep: 0
    maxTimePenalty: 0
    minCorrectPoints: 100
  oneStarScore: 270
  twoStarScore: 380
  threeStarScore: 600
  minScoreToUnlockNext: 380
  nextLevelId: level_2
  nextSceneName: Room2_InvestigationOffice
  lessons:
  - Connect a common scam outcome to the security principle it violates.
  - 'Recognize the common signs of a fake delivery text: unexpected, urgent, a small
    fee and an odd link.'
  - Name phishing and spot a lookalike domain.
  - 'Treat an OTP like a key: never share it, and verify callers through a channel
    you choose.'
  - Recognize that a request to disable security tools is a red flag.
  - Recognize that harmless-looking posts can collect personal data.
  learningSummary: 
  performanceHigh: 
  performanceModerate: 
  performanceLow: 
  tutorial: 1
  tutorialFirstQuestion: E03
